Phase D of android-handoever.md (D3), deliberately LAST after the de-gate commit: a stale --features android against a crate with no such feature is a hard cargo error, so the flag had to outlive the feature by exactly one commit. Removed $Android, its arg parse, and the if/else — one unconditional cargo build --release -p xpressclaw-cli. build.sh / build-signed.sh verified to contain no android references (they never gained the flag — that drift was part of the case for removing the feature, F2). Anyone with '.\build.ps1 --android' in muscle memory: the flag is now silently ignored by the switch (no match arm), which is fine — the build it produces is the android-capable one either way.
